Pluggable agent dispatcher: SDK / Mock / FileQueue

Refactors invokeAgent() to dispatch through an abstracted AgentDispatcher
rather than calling Anthropic SDK directly. Three implementations:

src/lib/agents/shared/dispatchers/types.ts
- AgentDispatcher interface with dispatch(req) -> response shape
- DispatchRequest with agent_id, tier, prompt, image (base64 OR path),
  user instruction, max tokens
- DispatchResponse with rawText + optional usage metrics
- DispatchError + DispatchTimeoutError exception classes

src/lib/agents/shared/dispatchers/sdk.ts (SdkDispatcher)
- Wraps current Anthropic SDK call. Production deploy use only.
  Requires ANTHROPIC_API_KEY. Preserves prompt-cache discipline
  (cache_control on system prompt).

src/lib/agents/shared/dispatchers/mock.ts (MockDispatcher)
- Fixture-based responses keyed by agent_id. Used for synthesis
  integration tests (per-agent unit tests already mock at agent-function
  level via vi.mock and don't need this layer).
- Supports string fixtures, sync function producers, async function
  producers — useful when test wants to capture request details.

src/lib/agents/shared/dispatchers/file-queue.ts (FileQueueDispatcher)
- THE STAGE 4 + SMOKE TEST DISPATCHER.
- Writes request JSON to .queue/requests/{requestId}.json
- Polls .queue/responses/{requestId}.json for the response
- Images persisted once to .queue/images/{sha256}.{ext}, dedupe by content
- Atomic file writes via temp + rename to prevent partial-read races
- Configurable poll interval, timeout, cleanup behavior
- Throws DispatchTimeoutError when no response in timeoutMs
- Validates response file requestId matches request

Claude Code session driver (next commit) reads request files, uses Task
tool to fulfill them, writes response files. Completely satisfies the
"all execution via Claude Code Max plan, no external API spend"
constraint from the original Stage 4 build authorization.

src/lib/agents/shared/dispatchers/index.ts
- getDefaultDispatcher() reads AGENT_DISPATCHER env var:
  unset/sdk -> SdkDispatcher | file-queue -> FileQueueDispatcher | mock -> MockDispatcher
- Cached per-process; rebuilt on env change
- _resetDispatcherCache() exposed for tests

src/lib/agents/shared/invoke.ts
- invokeAgent() now accepts optional `dispatcher` and `agentId` params
- Defaults to env-selected dispatcher (SDK by default, backwards compat)
- Existing 350-test suite passes unchanged because per-agent tests mock
  at @/lib/anthropic/client level and getDefaultDispatcher selects the
  cached SdkDispatcher which uses that mocked client

Tests: 18 new dispatcher tests
- file-queue.test.ts (8 tests): write request file + unblock on response,
  image persistence + dedup by sha256, timeout, cleanup behavior,
  cleanupAfterDispatch=false preservation, requestId mismatch rejection
- mock.test.ts (4 tests): fixture lookup, missing-fixture error,
  sync/async function producers
- index.test.ts (7 tests): all 3 selector branches, unknown mode error,
  cache hit, cache invalidation on mode change

.gitignore: exclude .queue/ runtime artifacts.

368 vitest passing total (350 before + 18 new).
TypeScript type-check clean.
Existing per-agent + orchestration tests UNCHANGED — proves backwards
compat.

Next: scripts/run-smoke-test.mjs FileQueue driver for chart-exemplar 09.
